  "segments": [
    {
      "id": "m14-s001",
      "speakerId": "m14-spk-a",
      "startMs": 0,
      "endMs": 4780,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Thanks everyone. This is the readout from the four-week chargeback discovery."
    },
    {
      "id": "m14-s002",
      "speakerId": "m14-spk-d",
      "startMs": 5030,
      "endMs": 11330,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "I'll start with the headline. Manual review takes about 18 minutes per dispute on average."
    },
    {
      "id": "m14-s003",
      "speakerId": "m14-spk-b",
      "startMs": 11580,
      "endMs": 14080,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Eighteen? I'd have guessed ten."
    },
    {
      "id": "m14-s004",
      "speakerId": "m14-spk-c",
      "startMs": 14330,
      "endMs": 17970,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "It's the evidence reading. Merchants send forty-page PDFs."
    },
    {
      "id": "m14-s005",
      "speakerId": "m14-spk-d",
      "startMs": 18220,
      "endMs": 26420,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "And 60 percent of the volume sits in just three reason codes: goods not received, duplicate processing, and cancelled recurring."
    },
    {
      "id": "m14-s006",
      "speakerId": "m14-spk-b",
      "startMs": 26670,
      "endMs": 31830,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "So if we automate those three, we cover most of the pain."
    },
    {
      "id": "m14-s007",
      "speakerId": "m14-spk-e",
      "startMs": 32080,
      "endMs": 38380,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "That's our recommendation. Start with the top three reason codes and prove it before widening."
    },
    {
      "id": "m14-s008",
      "speakerId": "m14-spk-b",
      "startMs": 38630,
      "endMs": 40750,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Wen, do you agree?"
    },
    {
      "id": "m14-s009",
      "speakerId": "m14-spk-c",
      "startMs": 41000,
      "endMs": 47680,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Yes. Those three are also the most rule-like. The judgement calls are in the long tail."
    },
    {
      "id": "m14-s010",
      "speakerId": "m14-spk-b",
      "startMs": 47930,
      "endMs": 53470,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Then that's the decision. We automate the top three dispute reason codes first."
    },
    {
      "id": "m14-s011",
      "speakerId": "m14-spk-a",
      "startMs": 53720,
      "endMs": 57360,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Great. For the build we'll need labelled data."
    },
    {
      "id": "m14-s012",
      "speakerId": "m14-spk-d",
      "startMs": 57610,
      "endMs": 63530,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "I'll build a labelled sample of 2,000 disputes by the end of the month."
    },
    {
      "id": "m14-s013",
      "speakerId": "m14-spk-c",
      "startMs": 63780,
      "endMs": 67420,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "I can have my team validate the labels."
    },
    {
      "id": "m14-s014",
      "speakerId": "m14-spk-a",
      "startMs": 67670,
      "endMs": 71690,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Wen, how does validation fit with your team's workload?"
    },
    {
      "id": "m14-s015",
      "speakerId": "m14-spk-c",
      "startMs": 71940,
      "endMs": 76340,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "It's tight. I report to Felix and we're already stretched."
    },
    {
      "id": "m14-s016",
      "speakerId": "m14-spk-b",
      "startMs": 76590,
      "endMs": 81370,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "I'll free up two analysts for two weeks. Wen, pick who."
    },
    {
      "id": "m14-s017",
      "speakerId": "m14-spk-c",
      "startMs": 81620,
      "endMs": 82980,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Thank you."
    },
    {
      "id": "m14-s018",
      "speakerId": "m14-spk-a",
      "startMs": 83230,
      "endMs": 86490,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Felix, how do you want progress reported?"
    },
    {
      "id": "m14-s019",
      "speakerId": "m14-spk-b",
      "startMs": 86740,
      "endMs": 91140,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "A spreadsheet with numbers. Not slides. I don't read slides."
    },
    {
      "id": "m14-s020",
      "speakerId": "m14-spk-a",
      "startMs": 91390,
      "endMs": 94270,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Understood. Weekly numbers in a spreadsheet."
    },
    {
      "id": "m14-s021",
      "speakerId": "m14-spk-e",
      "startMs": 94520,
      "endMs": 102340,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "From our side, Kwame leads the model work and JJ will help on the API once we get there."
    },
    {
      "id": "m14-s022",
      "speakerId": "m14-spk-b",
      "startMs": 102590,
      "endMs": 105090,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "What's the next decision point?"
    },
    {
      "id": "m14-s023",
      "speakerId": "m14-spk-a",
      "startMs": 105340,
      "endMs": 112780,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "When the labelled sample is done, we'll show a first model's accuracy and you decide on the build."
    },
    {
      "id": "m14-s024",
      "speakerId": "m14-spk-b",
      "startMs": 113030,
      "endMs": 115530,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Good. Clear gate, clear numbers."
    },
    {
      "id": "m14-s025",
      "speakerId": "m14-spk-a",
      "startMs": 115780,
      "endMs": 117140,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Thanks all."
    }
  ],
  "note": {
    "version": 1,
    "body": "# Gullwing chargeback discovery readout\n\n**Date:** April 9\n**Attendees:** Alex Rivera (Larkspur Labs), Priya Raman (Larkspur Labs), Kwame Mensah (Larkspur Labs), Felix Amundsen (Gullwing Payments), Wen Zhao (Gullwing Payments)\n\n## Summary\n\nReadout of the four-week discovery phase for Gullwing's chargeback automation.\n\n## Findings\n\n- Manual review takes about 18 minutes per dispute on average. Most of that time is spent reading merchant evidence, which often arrives as forty-page PDFs.\n- 60 percent of volume sits in three reason codes: goods not received, duplicate processing, and cancelled recurring.\n- Those three codes are also the most rule-like; the judgement calls are in the long tail.\n\n## Decisions\n\n- **Automate the top three dispute reason codes first**, and prove the approach before widening.\n- The next gate: once the labelled sample is complete, Larkspur presents a first model's accuracy and Felix decides on the build.\n\n## Action items\n\n- **Kwame Mensah** — build a labelled sample of 2,000 disputes by the end of the month.\n- **Wen Zhao** — have her team validate the labels; choose two analysts.\n- **Felix Amundsen** — free up two analysts for two weeks for label validation.\n- **Alex Rivera** — report weekly progress numbers in a spreadsheet.\n\n## Notes\n\n- Wen reports to Felix; the risk team is already stretched.\n- Felix wants numbers in a spreadsheet, not slides.\n- Kwame leads the model work; JJ will help on the API later.\n"
  },
